<<<
terza rima (Pros.); ‘third rhyme °. Dante’s metre in the Divina Commedia—lines of five iambic feet with an extra syllable, so rhymed that every rhyme occurs thrice in alternate lines, except the rhymes of the first & last lines of a canto, which occur twice only. In every tercet (see above) reckoned from the beginning,
